~ start
do start_talking()
do disable_movement()
do Flags.set_flag("forester.met")
Forester: So. You found the key.
- Why did you bury it? Why block the way at all?
	Forester: I hoped nobody would need to find it. That barricade wasn't spite. It was to keep something in.
	Forester: [wait=1] Past a certain point the forest is wrong, in a way that spreads if you let it get behind you.
- The blacksmith made you sound like a menace.
	Forester: [[Good.|That was rather the idea.|Let them talk.]] Better they fear an old man than go looking for what I'm guarding against.
	Forester: [wait=1] You're not the first past me. A stranger came through months back, asking odd questions about the trees. He never came back down.
Forester: The way on is past the rubble, if you're set on it. Mind yourself down there.
do stop_talking()
do enable_movement()
=> END

~ night
do start_talking()
Forester: [[Not now. I don't talk after dark, and you shouldn't walk.|The fire keeps it back. Stay in the light of it.|Sleep. It's worse at night, whatever it is.]]
do stop_talking()
=> END
